# A grammar that names one token both as `PLUS` and as `"+"` is rejected:
# the lexer's plus is one grammar symbol, so the other spelling's
# alternatives could never match.
# error: named_and_literal_terminal.grammar:20:8:
# error: "+" and PLUS are the same token (plus)
@lexer
tokens
    ident
    plus
    eof
    err
'+'                                         → plus
[a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z0-9_]*                      → ident
.                                           → err

@parser

top! = sum                                  → 1
sum  = IDENT PLUS IDENT                     → (named 1 3)
     | IDENT "+" IDENT "+" IDENT            → (lit 1 3 5)
